In article <3478.27359c0c@cc.nu.oz.au> c8730752@cc.nu.oz.au writes:
>Also, what about picking a limited number of items off the floor of the same 
>kind, eg, 1 of 2 orcs corpses. Even if I have the strenght to lift one, 
>the computer will try to pick up both which I don't have strenght for.

There isn't (that I know of) any easy way to pick up just one or two of
something.  However, if you can pick up *any* of them, and you try to, the
game will have you pick up as many of them as you can carry.  Thus, if 
there are 100 floating eye corpses on the ground, and you try to pick 
them up, you may find that you can only pick up 84 of them.  You can then
drop as many as you want to make room for other things (assuming the
floating eyes are 'q', d3q would drop 3 of them).

